WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.278
All right, thank you
so much, Sam. Shannon and I

00:00:08.278 --> 00:00:10.570
are going to be talking a
little bit about the thematic

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:13.180
and bootstrap lib
packages today.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.420
In short, these are new
packages to theme Shiny

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.492
as well as R Markdown and
traditional web content.

00:00:19.492 --> 00:00:20.950
And we're really
excited about kind

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.660
of the breadth of
what this can do

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.435
for theming and kind of the
ease of use to get started.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.080
So first off, introducing
these packages,

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.290
bootstrap lib or we're
calling bslib is really just

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:37.200
simplify theming of web
content via bootstrap.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.580
Now web content,
meaning could be Shiny,

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.210
could be R Markdown
and bootstrap,

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.380
as well as for
traditional web pages,

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:47.040
so there's a lot of power there.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.310
Thematic, on the other hand, is
kind of a complementary package

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.110
to bslib,
which is simplified

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.510
theming of our plots,
meaning ggplot,

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:57.480
lattice, base, and plot,

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.970
that is, kind of works in
conjunction with bslib.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.950
Both of these have
packagedown websites

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:05.920
where you can find out a
lot more info about them.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.922
Thematic is on CRAN
already and bslib is kind

00:01:08.922 --> 00:01:11.380
of waiting in the queue, so it
should hopefully be the next

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.058
few days.

00:01:12.058 --> 00:01:13.850
If you want to get
started with them today

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:16.720
you can always install the
dev versions from GitHub,

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.360
as you can see here with this
code. And a big thanks

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.360
to Carson Sievert who

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.283
let me adapt some of his slides
for today's presentation.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.700
He's one of the core
developers working

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.830
on both bootstrap lib
and thematic as part

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.830
of our Shiny team.

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.600
So first off, for
some folks, you

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.150
may have been using Shiny
before, you may have been using

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:37.510
R Markdown before, but less
people are kind of aware

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:39.880
of using bootstrap natively.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.650
And what this is,
is really just a lot

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.710
of CSS and JavaScript
plug-ins for front end web

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:46.330
development.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.930
You can dive deeper
into bootstrap

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:50.140
and we're going have a great
presentation about SASS,

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:53.548
which is using these variables
right after this presentation.

00:01:53.548 --> 00:01:55.090
But in short, this
is kind of working

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:57.413
behind the scenes in bslib and other packages

00:01:57.413 --> 00:01:59.830
and kind of provides you all
these nice things without you

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:02.400
having to know about it.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.730
So bootstrap lib is a wrapper
around custom bootstrap themes

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.820
and makes it really easy
to theme your documents

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:10.710
and use things
like SASS variables

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:13.590
without having to write all
this custom css out

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:14.490
of the box.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.128
Now, if you do
know those skills,

00:02:16.128 --> 00:02:18.420
and if you gain those skills
from someone like Appsilon,

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:19.980
or have them working
with you, they

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.810
can further expand
your applications

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:24.240
with css  or sass variables.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.610
But again, this is
really kind of an R

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.590
interface and
functions where you

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:32.060
don't have to know all
of it to get started.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:34.040
And again, you've been
using components of this

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.230
through Shiny and
RMarkdown for years,

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:39.350
you just probably
didn't know it.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.690
So to start using
bslib, it's

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.460
really just a
one function call,

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:47.100
so we have a very basic Shiny
app here for the UI component.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.615
And we're also going to load
the bslib package.

00:02:49.615 --> 00:02:51.740
So we can call fluidPage,
although it could really

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.630
be any component of Shiny.

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:59.030
And the theme argument will
take bs underscore theme as the argument.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.697
So this will provide
an interface to bslib

00:03:01.697 --> 00:03:03.530
and all the different
theming components

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:06.650
you could do, like
background, foreground, fonts,

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.560
changing all these different
components in bulk on the page

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.780
without having to
write individual css

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.670
for each item.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.640
So fluidPage, navbarPage,
bootstrapPage,

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.590
all these different
things have the same kind

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:21.440
of theme equals bs_theme argument.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:24.110
And again, you may have been
using this theme argument,

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:26.600
something like Shiny themes
or writing your own custom

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.160
bootstraps css.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:31.010
Boostrap theme is more
powerful kind of in our minds,

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.050
because you are
providing, again,

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:35.420
sass variables and all
the niceties of bootstrap

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:39.230
in there again, to the
power or the ease of use,

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.880
kind of both balance together.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:46.540
Now, something to note here is
that for for bootstrap users,

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:48.610
this is moving
from bootstrap 3, to

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:51.400
bootstrap 4, which is
a more modern, more recent

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.320
implementation of bootstrap.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.760
So there is some compatibility
layers here that should help

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.610
most Shiny apps just
work out of the box

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:00.280
snd upgrade to bootstrap 4.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.560
However, if you have
some legacy applications,

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:03.500
you could always try

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:07.480
version equals 3 here in the
best argument if it is kind

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.420
of messing with your
overall theming.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.830
But for new applications, just
stick to bootstrap 4.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.440
Again, a more recent version

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:19.459
and that'll be the
code recommendation.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:22.710
You know, in terms of bootstrap 3
versus boostrap 4 for looks,

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:25.320
like really it's hard
to tell the difference,

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:28.350
you might see it here in
terms of like this blue is

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:30.900
a slightly lighter, the fonts
or a little bit different,

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.980
maybe not as bold, really

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:35.040
most of the benefits
are behind the scenes,

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.990
like just switching
from version 3 to 4

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:41.160
might give you this more
slightly modern looking feel,

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.670
but it's not going to change
the core of your application

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:47.300
just with the base theme.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.090
But there are, again, lots of
things built in there that it's

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:51.270
worth upgrading to four.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.010
To preview a theme
and actually get

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:59.520
into some of the bulk of what
these themes can do for you,

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:03.660
you can call this new function
from bslib bs underscore theme

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:04.980
underscore preview.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.803
And this will take bs_theme
as an argument,

00:05:06.803 --> 00:05:08.970
and you can provide either
custom themes that you've

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:12.270
built yourself or full
boot swatch themes which

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:14.430
are essentially open
source free themes

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:16.410
that other people have created.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:18.810
So you can see with
essentially one line of code,

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:20.910
we've taken this basic
Shiney application

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.010
in themed every component of it.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.530
So the fonts are different.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:26.950
This is perpetuated into
all of the dropdown.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:31.710
So the date, the select inputs,
date ranges, the slider bars,

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:35.760
all of those with respect to the
right colors, the right fonts

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.310
and other components
that you're changing,

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:41.920
as well as the kind of
pop-ups or action buttons.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:46.240
So primary, secondary warnings,
danger buttons, accent colors.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.640
Again, all of this is changing
kind of in bulk and together

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:52.620
in a unified interface.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.810
So if you want to just use
one of these bootswatch

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:57.143
themes out of the box, they're
going to be very powerful

00:05:57.143 --> 00:05:58.530
and should be very pretty.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:00.030
A lot of them have
been kind of used

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:02.130
for front end
development for years.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:04.770
But you can also
kind of customize

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:08.340
wide portions of your app
with things like sass variables

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:11.650
or other functions
built into bootstrap.

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:14.150
So, again, while I've kind of
hit on this a couple of times,

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:15.817
I really want to
protect people in terms

00:06:15.817 --> 00:06:17.990
of don't be scared if
there's things in here

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:20.495
that you haven't seen before,
if you want to learn those,

00:06:20.495 --> 00:06:22.370
you'll be even more
powerful, but they're not

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:24.830
necessary to use it.

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:27.080
So if you did want to dive
deeper into sass again,

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.160
there's going to be
a presentation right

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:29.310
after this about it.

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:33.320
And there is some documentation
about the sass, R wrapper

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:38.898
for R packages that will let you
kind of learn how to use those.

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.940
In short, I'm not going
to read this whole thing,

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.970
but sass is really a meta
language on top of css.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.850
So you think of css, it's
changing individual components,

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:50.390
sass would kind of provide a more
elegant or systematic syntax,

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:52.930
letting you change multiple
things at one time.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.430
This usually leads to more
manageable stylesheets

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:59.010
or styling in general.

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:01.650
So I mentioned earlier that
you can create your own theme,

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:03.990
so we showed a pre-built
bootswatch theme.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:06.330
Now we're using essentially
the same argument, so

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:09.900
bootstrap theme, but
we're kind of mandating

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.150
what specific components
we want to change.

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:14.940
So, again, this theme may not
be the most pretty thing to you.

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:18.450
I kind of made it a little
bit garish, just a pop out.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:20.130
But you can see the
background is grey,

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:21.270
the foreground is black.

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:23.040
So we have a background
of gray and then

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.840
the thought will be in black.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.360
The primary color is
this lovely purple, which

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:28.540
goes along with R-Ladies,

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:32.070
and I really do like it, maybe
not with this grey theme.

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:34.410
And then we change the
base font to Francis,

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:36.820
which is kind of, again,
a very different font.

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:39.240
And you can see that the
fonts perpetuated into each

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:40.860
of the different sections.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:44.040
So, yeah, I don't really
love Frances's as a theme

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:45.960
or as the font, but
you can see that each

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:48.270
of the different parts
are changing, which

00:07:48.270 --> 00:07:51.680
is the part to highlight here.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:55.220
You might also notice that I
didn't have to load externally

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:58.430
a different font, I just said,
pull in this Google font

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:01.310
process, and I could change
it to anything I want.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:04.400
And it will automatically
pull in the style css

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.560
and the Google font,
download it and load it

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:08.030
in your application.

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:11.190
So making it really easy
to import Google Fonts.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.815
And there's hundreds
of different ones.

00:08:12.815 --> 00:08:14.940
You could use here, as well
as the most common ones

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:15.700
used in web dev.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.520
If we switch over
to probably a better

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.980
pilot in terms of not
one I created randomly,

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.710
but one that's based on
something like material dark,

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:28.320
you can again see that we've
changed all the components

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:28.840
at once.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.070
So the backgrounds change.

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.820
The foreground is still
this lovely purple.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.720
And then we have a new font.

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:36.909
This time, fira sans,
which is one font.

00:08:36.909 --> 00:08:38.880
But I actually really
do like and again, it's

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:40.770
perpetuating this
into the slider's,

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:43.570
into all the different
components all at once.

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:46.860
And with minimal code, I'm able
to create a robustly themed

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:49.070
application.

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:52.640
We'll go over a demo of what
all these different things are,

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:55.010
in short, like this screenshot
shows you the bulk of it,

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:57.993
but you can use Bootstrap
preview with this

00:08:57.993 --> 00:09:00.410
to show what plots will look
like, what tables would look

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.240
like, notifications,
different fonts,

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:03.680
and you can actually
customize it

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.930
live inside the Shiny
application, which

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:08.440
is really cool.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.570
And so I will show
you that right

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:13.810
now in terms of what
the preview looks like,

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:16.220
may pull us over here.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:19.730
So if I again, I'm
inside RStudio,

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:22.970
I'm just going to pull up this
chunk of here. So bootstrap theme

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:26.030
preview and then providing
it with some arguments

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:29.220
to the bootstrapping component.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:32.280
So if I run this, it'll
load the Shiny application,

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:38.120
I'll make that full screen
in a second to spin up.

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:40.970
And now here is my
kind of Matrix themed

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:42.260
Shiny application.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.030
So, again, all the
different buttons work.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:47.450
And I can change
things like the font.

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:50.540
So maybe I don't want fair
armano and I want loto.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:52.290
I can close that out.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:54.830
And it will change the fonts.

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:58.100
I can go to accent
colors and say, well, I

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.630
don't want the primary
color to be green.

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:02.780
Let's do a f0f0f0

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:06.350
and we'll make it like a white
background or primary color.

00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:08.630
And now everything
is here and white.

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:15.060
I can go over to plots and
do let it load for a second.

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:19.740
My CPU is getting some pressure
from me, from the web screen

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.520
or webcasting.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:24.430
So the plots here
are perpetuated

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:26.180
and have those themed as well.

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:30.550
The tables are themed to match
the background notifications,

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:32.140
all these different things.

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:34.435
So, again, as you're
kind of playing around

00:10:34.435 --> 00:10:36.310
with different themes,
and want to change them.

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:37.780
You have this
ability to see what

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.905
all the different components
of an application look

00:10:39.905 --> 00:10:42.790
like without having to write
all this different code just

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:43.810
to test it.

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:46.480
You can obviously, like, run
up your actual production

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:49.550
application locally and see
how it looks with a theming.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:52.590
But this allows you to
change things really quickly.

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:54.750
All right, so it
closed down that

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.833
and go back into the slides.

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:04.220
You can also use bslib
with R Markdown now,

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:06.140
this is somewhat
experimental today

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:08.658
in terms of it is it's
been focused on Shiny

00:11:08.658 --> 00:11:10.950
I think that's really what
we want to talk about today is

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:13.430
Shiny but you can imagine
that there are also

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:16.730
R Markdown documents that
have a Shiny runtime or just

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.630
R Markdown documents
you're generating

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:20.660
and you want to
theme those as well.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:23.330
So one of the versions
of R Markdown that

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:26.430
should be merged soon allows
for theme arguments.

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:28.820
So you can change again, the
background, the foreground,

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:32.540
the primary, the base
font, very similar to what

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:35.060
you're doing with your
bstheme theme argument

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:37.190
in Shiny proper.

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:39.620
If you don't want to ride out
the whole theming component

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:41.690
yourself, you can
again get access

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:43.170
to all the boot swatch theme.

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:45.680
So something like solar, you
can pull that in automatically

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:47.630
by name.

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:50.360
And while I'm really excited
about the future of R Markdown,

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:53.000
this is still more
experimental in R Markdown

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:56.000
and you'd have to install this
GitHub version of R Markdown

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.290
to test it out.

00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:59.870
So maybe wait a little bit
for R Markdown theming,

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:01.310
but Shiny theming
is really going

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:03.020
to be ready in the
next few days, which

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:04.160
is very, very exciting.

00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:10.670
Again, for using some of the
bootswatch themes for Shiny

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:14.450
proper in the past, this was
through the shinythemes

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:15.180
package.

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:18.410
So you would load like
solar or darkly or menti,

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:21.320
all these different boot swatch
themes which are listed here

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:24.110
in terms of there's a
full list of, I think, two

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:27.290
or three dozen different
themes you can use.

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:29.180
This is just going to
be loaded with bootswatch,

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:32.270
and then naming it
within whatever fluid component

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:34.720
you have.

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:37.150
There are some newer
themes from bootswatch 4

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:39.490
that weren't
available previously,

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:42.280
and so we are switching
to bootstrap four.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.908
So if you want to
use an older theme,

00:12:43.908 --> 00:12:45.700
you could look at older
themes, but there's

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:50.270
some newer ones as well,
that are really, really cool.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:55.190
Awesome OK, so we've kind of
got over a bunch of things that

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:57.200
are themable, I'm going
to turn over to Shannon

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:59.330
here in a second to walk
through thematic, which

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:02.710
is the complimentary package
to bslib, but things

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:03.960
that are currently themable

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:05.585
And the next CRAN
release, which again,

00:13:05.585 --> 00:13:07.700
should be the next few
days, the Shiny package

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:10.640
proper R Markdown HTML document

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:13.550
as long as you have that
specific GitHub version,

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:17.070
DT data tables, which are
perpetuated through Shiny.

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:20.360
And then really any bootstrap
compatible HTML, CSS.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:24.020
So you can add to this
and add other stylesheets

00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:26.757
that are bootstrap compatible.

00:13:26.757 --> 00:13:28.340
Some of the other
things that are soon

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:30.590
to be themeable and that the dev
team is working on,

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:33.530
it would love your help in terms
of open source contributions

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:35.480
or asks or different
things that are

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:38.990
working on some of the other
HTML-based R Markdown output

00:13:38.990 --> 00:13:39.630
formats.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:42.620
So beyond just a
document, additionally,

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:45.800
a lot of the HTML widgets have
to be perpetuated through.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.960
So plotly will work
through ggplotly.

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:50.600
But in terms of plotly
proper, reactable,

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:54.587
which is a package similar
to DT for reactive tables.

00:13:54.587 --> 00:13:56.420
And in some of the other
extension packages,

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:59.330
like shiny widgets that
provide additional widgets that

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:02.660
are not in Shiny proper.

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:05.510
One of the things that's
fundamentally un-themable

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:10.670
via css and therefore
bootstrap or sass or bslib

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:14.490
is plotOutput or essentially
R based graphics.

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:18.320
So lattice, ggplot,
base R, those are

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:21.410
images, not css in
the classical sense,

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:23.720
where you can change the
components, they're generated

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:27.350
by R. So the way to
get around that is

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:30.380
to use thematic, which
actually translates the CSS

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:33.680
components into these R plots.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:35.870
So in this case,
we'll use thematic

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:38.630
to further extend the
theme from bslib

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:41.240
into things like
plotting components.

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:42.920
I'm about to be
turning over to Shannon

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:45.565
and she's going to be walking
through the thematic portions.

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:53.440
Yeah, so once you've gotten
your Shiny application

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:57.490
or R Markdown down beautifully
styled with bslib,

00:14:57.490 --> 00:14:59.980
one thing that you'll notice
is that the plots are not

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:03.490
automatically styling the
way that Tom just mentioned.

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:06.040
And so that's where you're
going to want to use thematic,

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:08.020
because once you've
gotten that really

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:09.700
nice look to your
Shiny application,

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:13.600
you're going to want to pass
that on to your R plots as well.

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:16.430
So that's where thematic
comes to the rescue.

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:19.690
And what you can
do inside of Shiny

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:23.410
is use this function
thematic underscore shiny,

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:27.700
and you see that we
have that theme set

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:29.330
inside the Shiny application.

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:32.260
And now that setting
is being passed

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:35.990
on to the plots inside
of our Shiny application.

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:37.250
So thematic is giving

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:41.440
those R plots the ability
to translate, as Tom mentions,

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:45.890
the custom styling of the Shiny
application into our styling

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:48.970
and give that plot a very
cohesive look with the rest

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:50.300
of the Shiny application.

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:57.280
So what the thematic
package in general does

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:00.200
is that it changes the
default of the R plots.

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:03.250
And you can use
that thematic underscore shiny

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:05.560
function to turn
the customization

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.190
to the plots on inside Shiny.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:10.570
But you can also use
a function called thematic underscore on

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.580
to turn it on globally.

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:16.870
And if you do that, you can
also, within that function,

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:21.370
set the specific background,
foreground, and accent colors

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:23.210
that you want for the plots.

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:27.370
So you can set the
theming of the plot there.

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:28.930
And the other thing
that you can do

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:30.790
is that you can
actually set the font

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:34.120
and we have set the
font here to indie flower

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:37.840
and indie flower is
actually a Google font.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:39.760
What thematic does
that's really cool

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:43.180
is that it will automatically
download, cache, and register

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:44.830
with R any Google
font that you

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:46.450
want to use inside your R plots.

00:16:52.127 --> 00:16:53.710
The other thing that
thematic can do

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:56.590
is in the slide before
this, we customize

00:16:56.590 --> 00:17:01.270
the theme of each of the
plots, but we can also, thematic

00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:03.550
will also just grab
the auto theming

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:07.930
so it will detect what
the HTML container settings are

00:17:07.930 --> 00:17:11.900
of the plot and it'll apply
those to your R plot.

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:16.099
And what that looks like
inside of an RStudio session.

00:17:16.099 --> 00:17:18.130
So if you've
turned thematic on,

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:21.280
if you run that function
and you're in RStudio

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:23.650
and you have a
custom appearance,

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:25.750
you're RStudio themes
that is going to auto

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:27.520
detect that RStudio theme.

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:30.280
So you get this actually really
nice look inside your RStudio

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:33.310
session where the plot is
actually looking again,

00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:37.830
cohesive with your
RStudio session.

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:39.780
And then similarly,
it'll do that same thing

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:42.390
where it'll automatically
detect your R

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:44.850
Markdown down settings
or your Shiny settings,

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:49.020
and so if you have
used bs underscore theme

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:51.780
and customized your
Shiny application,

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:55.470
the auto detection, the auto
theming inside thematic

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:58.200
is going to be able
to apply the settings,

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:01.440
the aesthetics that you've
set for your Shiny application

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:02.480
to your plots.

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:08.940
So why this matters,
because it's

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:11.910
going to help you to
create really cohesive,

00:18:11.910 --> 00:18:15.900
beautiful R Markdown and
Shiny applications after you've

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.450
spent all that time customizing
the look of your applications

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:19.720
of your own Markdown report

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:21.270
thematic is going
to let you easily

00:18:21.270 --> 00:18:23.790
apply those settings
to your plots

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:26.700
to, again, make everything
look really nice and cohesive.

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:30.090
You can still use
traditional theme settings

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:32.520
inside ggplot
for one-off plots,

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:34.200
but what thematic
will let you do is,

00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:36.330
is apply that to
the whole document,

00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:39.180
the whole application,
or to all of the plots

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:41.340
that you're making in
RStudio if you want to.

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:43.007
And with that, I'm
going to hand it over

00:18:43.007 --> 00:18:47.050
to Tom, who's going to show you
some of thematic in action.

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:51.280
Perfect thanks so much, yeah,
so as Shannon mentioned,

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:52.660
you can use it
with R Markdown,

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:54.080
you can use inside Shiny

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:55.840
and then it will
also work directly

00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:58.240
within kind of just an
interactive session.

00:18:58.240 --> 00:18:59.000
So here

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:02.350
I'm going to load the thematic
